THE DIFFERENTIAL DECIDED THE FIRST CUT, and found something no unit test would. codex-luna
produced 91 lines of output and one was out of order:

    shell:  wtalloc, wt-provision, wt-select
    codex:  wt-provision, wt-select, wtalloc

The shell's glob sorts by locale collation, which ignores the punctuation, so `wtalloc` compares
as `wtallocation`-ish against `wtprovision` and `a` precedes `p`. codex-luna sorted byte-wise,
where `-` (0x2D) precedes `a` (0x61). One line in 91, in a wire format the autopilot greps.

THE CRITIQUE DECIDED THE SECOND, and found what the differential structurally could not.
codex-luna on glm-53-flash, claim 1, verified by running all three against a fake `pgrep`:

    shell:          dispatcher processes: 7
    claude-sonnet:  dispatcher processes: 7
    glm-53-flash:   dispatcher processes: NOT MEASURED: pgrep printed a non-count: "7\nextra"

fb-status.sh pipes pgrep through `head -1` and takes the first line; glm-53-flash refuses the
whole value. The differential rated both arms "agrees" because that branch only runs when NO
agent is live, and one was. A case the oracle cannot reach is exactly what the subjective tier is
for, and this is the clearest instance of it yet: the differential and the critique each caught a
defect the other could not.

Its claim 2 is FALSE, and checked rather than assumed: it alleged glm discards write errors and
"returns the bd-derived status, potentially 0 or 1" where the shell exits 141. Measured, all
three exit 141 -- the script's own `head` closes a pipe and pipefail propagates SIGPIPE, and both
arms reproduce it. One true claim and one false one from the same critic in the same file.

Its JUDGEMENT is right and applies to the WINNER too: the collation key hardcodes one glibc
en_US.UTF-8 ordering and only the alphabet currently observed. An uppercase task name or a new
punctuation character would reorder the report with no code change and no diagnostic. That is a
real limitation of the merged code, not a reason to prefer another arm, and it is recorded here
rather than fixed today.

Verified after merge, both sides run fresh: stdout IDENTICAL line for line, exit 141 from both,
and the pgrep-multiline branch now agrees too. 1303 tests, clippy 9.
